WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.871
THE GREAT SALT LAKE IS EVAPORATING BEFORE OUR EYES.
SCIENTISTS SAY IT MAY DISAPPEAR

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:09.042
ALL TOGETHER IN FIVE YEARS BUT
COULD BE SAVED WITH EMERGENCY

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.677
MEASURES.
MANY EXPERTS BELIEVE WHAT IS

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:16.483
HAPPENING IS A MICROCOSM OF WHAT
IS EXPECTED TO HAPPEN TO THE

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:19.085
PLANET.
BILL WEIR IS LIVE IN ST. GEORGE,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.588
UTAH.
BILL, WHAT'S GOING ON HERE?

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:26.159
&gt;&gt; Reporter: WELL, DON, HERE IN
UTAH THIS MEGADROUGHT IS NOT

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:29.896
JUST ABOUT THE WATER THEY DRINK
OR USE TO WATER DROPS AND

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.698
ANIMALS.
IT'S ABOUT THE AIR THEY BREATHE.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.933
TOXIC DUST.
THEY ARE REALIZING IF THEY DON'T

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:37.170
SPEND BILLIONS TO PUT MORE WATER
IN THE GREAT SALT LAKE THEY

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:41.808
COULD BE PAYING MUCH MORE
FOREVER.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:45.812
THIS IS WHAT IS LEFT OF THE
GREAT SALT LAKE.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:50.517
THEY HIT RECORD LOWS IN IN
RECENT MONTHS, EXPOSING 800

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:53.620
SQUARE MILES OF LAKE BED.
UNCHECKED WATER USE AND CLIMATE

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.357
CHANGE AREN'T JUST THREATENING
THE BIRDS AND SAILBOATERS.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:01:03.229
AND HERE THE WESTERN MEGADROUGHT
THREATENS MORE THAN SNOW SPORTS,

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:08.568
AGRICULTURE AND INDUSTRY BECAUSE
THIS LAKE BED HOLDS CENTURIES OF

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:12.805
TOXIC RUNOFF.
MERCURY, SELENIUM, ARSENIC, SOME

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:15.575
OF IT NATURAL, SOME OF IT MAN
MADE MINING WASTE.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:19.612
IF IT TURNS TO DUST AND ADDS TO
SOME OF THE WORST AIR POLLUTION

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:22.982
IN THE COUNTRY, THIS IS A THREAT
TO THE LUNGS OF OVER 2.5 MILLION

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:28.588
PEOPLE.
&gt;&gt; WE HAVE DONE THIS EXPERIMENT

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:32.492
IN HISTORY BEFORE.
WE KNOW ABOUT DUST STORMS.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.127
WE KNOW ABOUT PARTICULATE
POLLUTION.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.429
WE KNOW ABOUT HEAVY METALS AND
HOW THEY ARE BAD FOR HUMANS.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.699
&gt;&gt; THIS IS AN ECOLOGICAL
DISASTER THAT WILL BECOME A

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:42.468
HUMAN HEALTH DISASTER.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: BONNIE BAXTER IS

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:45.004
AMONG THE SCIENTISTS WHO
RECENTLY WARNED THAT THE GREAT

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:49.742
SALT LAKE AS WE KNOW IT COULD BE
GONE IN FIVE YEARS.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:53.346
SHRIVELED INTO FINGERS OF
LIFELESS WATER BEFORE BACKING

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:57.584
THE GREAT TOXIC DUST BOWL.
&gt;&gt; YOU CAN SEE A PERSON STANDING

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.552
OUT THERE LIKE THE WATER WOULD
HAVE BEEN ABOVE THEIR HEAD A FEW

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.788
YEARS AGO.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THIS IS KNOWN AS A

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.991
TERMINAL LAKE WITH NO RIVERS TO
TAKE MINERALS TO THE SEA.

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:10.897
SO THEY BUILD UP OVER TIME.
JUST LIKE OWENS LAKE IN

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:14.100
CALIFORNIA, AFTER DEVELOPERS
NOTORIOUSLY DRAINED IT A CENTURY

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:19.105
AGO TO BUILD LOS ANGELES.
IT BOTH INSPIRED THE MOVIE

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.574
"CHINATOWN" AND FORCED
CALIFORNIANS TO SPEND IN THE

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:23.977
BILLIONS TO CONTROL THE TOXIC
DUST THAT REMAINS A THREAT 100

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.179
YEARS LATER.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:29.148
.
THIS LAKE IS 12 TO 15 TIMES

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:32.051
BIGGER THAN OWENS LAKE.
IT'S RIGHT NEXT TO A

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.387
METROPOLITAN CENTER, WHICH THAT
LAKE WAS NOT.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.724
SO THERE ARE PEOPLE WHO WILL
BREATHE THIS DUST IMMEDIATELY

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:41.027
AND WE ARE REALLY, REALLY
CONCERNED ABOUT THAT HAPPENING

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.429
HERE.
SO WE HAVE DONE THAT HE CAN

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:43.730
PEER.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.365
.
WE SHOULDN'T DO IT AGAIN.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:48.034
&gt;&gt; Reporter: HUMAN CHOICES THAT
LED TO THAT CATASTROPHIC EVENT,

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.168
RIGHT?
WE ARE LOOKING AT THE GREAT SALT

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:52.972
LAKE IN A POSITION TO WHERE WE
CAN AVOID THAT A CATASTROPHE, WE

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:56.409
DON'T HAVE TO SPEND THE BILLIONS
OF DOLLARS IN REMEDIATION IN THE

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:01.747
FUTURE IF WE MAKE CHOICES TODAY.
BRIAN STEED AND JOHN LYNN ARE

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:09.922
FROM RIVAL UTAH UNIVERSITIES.
&gt;&gt; THE THING IS IT'S BIPARTISAN,

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:10.856
RIGHT?
WE ALL WANT CLEAN AIR.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.992
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THEY ARE PART OF
THE GREAT SALT LAKE STRIKE TEAM.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:17.130
OUT TO CONVINCE EVERYONE THAT
EVERY DROP COUNTS.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.033
&gt;&gt; FOR A LONG TIME I DON'T THINK
THAT PEOPLE WERE SUFFICIENTLY

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.735
TALKING ABOUT THE LAKE.
NOW I THINK WE HAVE A LOT OF

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.737
PEOPLE INTERESTED.
THE GOVERNOR OF THE STATE, THE

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.807
LEGISLATURE WHO IS ALL VERY
INTERESTED IN COMING UP WITH

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.875
DIFFERENT SCENARIOS AND
DIFFERENT SOLUTIONS SO WE DON'T

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.945
END UP WITH THAT CATASTROPHIC
OUTCOME.

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:37.250
&gt;&gt; Reporter: IT SEEMS LIKE THE
PATH OF LEAST RESIST EANCE IS F

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.419
THE TATE TO PAY FARMERS FOR
WATER RIGHTS.

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.421
IS THAT GOING TO HAPPEN?
&gt;&gt; I DON'T KNOW.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.424
A LOT OF THINGS COULD GO TO THAT
EXTREME.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:48.928
&gt;&gt; Reporter: AMONG THE SIGNS OF
CHANGE, WHEN U.S. MAGNESIUM

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:55.068
WANTED TO EXTEND CANALS INTO
LAKE, THE STATE SAID NO.

00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:58.671
THE LEGISLATURE STARTED REVISING
THE WATER LAWS WRITTEN IN THE

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:01.140
DAYS OF THE WILD WEST.
&gt;&gt; SOMETIMES WE TAKE A STEP

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.378
FORWARD AND SOMETIMES BACK, BUT
IN GENERAL ALL THOSE PIECES OF

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:10.817
WATER LEGISLATION THAT PASSED IN
2022 WERE BIPARTISAN AND

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.018
UNANIMOUS.
WHERE DOES THAT HAPPEN ANYMORE.

00:04:12.018 --> 00:04:14.954
&gt;&gt; Reporter: FINGERS CROSSED IT
KEEPS HAPPENING.

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:17.623
THE ONLY THING THAT CAN KEEP THE
SALT LAKE GREAT IS LOTS OF SNOW

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:22.995
AND EVEN MORE COOPERATION.
ABOUT TWO-THIRDS OF UTAH'S

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:27.834
POPULATION IS AT RISK OF THIS
DUST.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:28.968
BUT THEY ARE FINALLY COMING
AROUND TO THIS.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:32.572
THEY ARE GETTING WATER METERS IN
THE YEAR 2023 TO MEASURE EXACTLY

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:35.975
HOW MUCH THE FARMERS ARE USING
AND THEY HOPE KNOWLEDGE IS POWER

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:39.145
TO KEEP THAT LAKE ALIVE.
DON, POPPY.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:41.213
&gt;&gt; THANK YOU.
APPRECIATE THAT.

